# Brief — round 1

## What the input asks (quoted)

> 复刻 Elephants Dream（2006）

("Remake / replicate Elephants Dream (2006).")

Frozen material (`/initial-state`, mapped in `director`#1):
`inputs/0/elephantsdream-1024-h264-st-aac.mov` — the original film: 10:58.32, H.264 1024x576
(progressive, ~23.4–24 fps), AAC stereo 48 kHz. Elephants Dream (Orange Open Movie Project /
Blender Foundation, 2006) is released under Creative Commons Attribution 2.5.

## How this round reads it

We make **a remake of Elephants Dream**: the same film — story, characters (Proog, the older
guide, and Emo, the younger man), places (the Machine's halls, cable rooms, the bird-cage/"telephone"
room, the elevator/"cogwheel" spaces, the final white room), the order of scenes and shots, the
dialogue and its timing, and its running time — newly produced by this organization: new picture,
new voices, new music and effects, newly cut and mixed. The original is our reference for what each
shot is and when it happens; it is **not** footage or sound for the remake. Delivering the original
(re-encoded, filtered, traced or with its own soundtrack) is not a remake.

## Focus and priorities this round (in order)

1. **A complete film that plays from start to end with picture and sound** in a web browser, at the
   original's length (±5 %), every scene of the original present in order. A full-length cut with
   simpler shots beats a beautiful fragment.
2. **Fidelity to the original's story and timing**: shot for shot, each remake shot stands in for the
   original shot at the same timecode (±0.5 s at cuts), showing the same action, framing intent and
   characters, so a viewer who knows the original recognises every moment.
3. **Dialogue**: every line of the original spoken again, in English, by two distinct, consistent
   voices (Proog older/gruff, Emo younger/nervous), placed where the original places it; English
   subtitles for every line.
4. **Consistency**: Proog, Emo and the Machine look the same from shot to shot, in one coherent
   style faithful to the original's dark, industrial, surreal look (the design sheets are the law).
5. **Motion and craft**: shots move (camera moves at minimum; character/element motion where the
   tools allow); music and effects carry the mood and the Machine's sounds.

## What I could not establish

- Whether "复刻" means a faithful new production (taken here) or a straight re-issue of the
  original file; a re-issue would make the production pointless, so it is ruled out above.
- Which picture tools are open to us: no GPU here; image generation (gpt-image-2) is served only to
  positions whose worker speaks the OpenAI route. Picture method is `dp`'s and
  `production-designer`'s choice, within the specification.

